# ReadBoot editorial terminology (glossary)

Use **print / editorial** language in **Storybook** `parameters.docs`, **UI** comments, **`HOMEPAGE_CONTENT.md`**, and marketing copy—the same vocabulary fits **magazine-style** and full-bleed layouts. **Code** (`BoxedFeatureHero`, `FullBleedHero`, PascalCase files where present) stays per `ui-atomic-architecture.mdc`. This file is the **glossary SSOT**; a future public “Glossary” page in docs/Storybook can mirror it.

**Visual default:** **`readboot-branding.mdc`** — prefer **full-bleed, seamless, light chrome**. Terms like **boxed** or **frame** describe a *pattern* or legacy component, **not** a rule to put heavy borders on everything.

## 1. Section boundary (the “hero” / band wrapper)

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Boxed / inset** | Content lives inside a **visible rule** (charcoal frame)—“system break,” coupon, framed story. |
| **Open / floating** | Elements sit **on newsprint** with **no** containing rule around the **whole** band (editorial flow). |
| **Full-bleed (media)** | Image or color **runs to the viewport edge**—splash / high-impact (distinct from “open text band”). |
| **Frame / framed** | The **rule** itself; a story **in** a frame is **framed**. |

**Legacy heroes (patterns library):** **`BoxedFeatureHero`** = boxed band; **`FullBleedHero`** = **open** portrait + type stack. **Greenfield:** prefer **open / full-bleed** shells without a thick outer rule unless the design asks for a framed block.

## 2. Headline hierarchy

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Banner / streamer** | Massive head **across full width**. |
| **Skyline** | Horizontal strip **at top** (often above nameplate)—teasers. |
| **Kicker** | Short line **above** the main head (context). |
| **Deck / drop head** | Summary line **below** the main headline. |
| **Hammer** | Very large **1–3 word** line **above** a smaller main headline. |

## 3. Layout architecture

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Modular** | Stories/images in **distinct rectangles**; modern grid. |
| **Gutter** | Vertical **space** between type and image (or columns). |
| **L-wrap / side-saddle** | Type beside image; **L-shaped** flow (e.g. portrait + column). |
| **Dutch wrap** | One column **taller** than the head beside it. |
| **Tombstoning** | **Avoid:** two same-size heads **adjacent**—reads like grave markers. |

## 4. Branding & utility

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Flag / nameplate** | Title / logo strip (“ReadBoot” on the paper). |
| **Ear** | Small promo/CTA **corner** at top of front page. |
| **Folio** | Page/date/section **meta** line (often top or bottom). |
| **Pull quote** | Body sentence **lifted** and enlarged for emphasis. |

## 5. Hero components (code ↔ metaphor)

| Component | Metaphor |
|-----------|----------|
| **`ReadBootBand`** | Single hero band; use **`surface`** (boxed vs open) — see layout model. |
| **`BoxedFeatureHero`** | Preset: boxed / framed band (`surface="boxed"`). |
| **`FullBleedHero`** | Preset: open band on newsprint (kicker, deck, lead); **not** full-bleed *splash* unless you add edge media (`surface="open"`). |

## 6. SCSS Modules (implementation)

- Prefer **local** roots: e.g. `.rootBoxed`, `.rootOpen`, `.sideSaddle`, or `data-layout="boxed"|"open"`, not global `hero--boxed` unless one wrapper owns the class.
- **Charcoal** rules use design tokens (`readboot-branding.mdc`).

## 7. Do / don’t

- **Do** use this vocabulary in docs and comments; call out **tombstoning** when reviewing two-up heads.
- **Don’t** use newspaper terms as **variable names**—keep PascalCase component names.

